# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Validated scenarios (tested against IOF Core 202603 and CCO v2.0 parses)
#
# These confirm the cascade handles the critical topologies correctly:
#
#   CCO-aligned         DomainClass ⊑ cco:Artifact ⊑ ... ⊑ BFO:material entity
#   CCO-aligned         DomainClass ⊑ cco:FrequencyProfile ⊑ BFO_0000144  (cco: caught before BFO_0000144)
#   IOF-aligned         DomainClass ⊑ iof:Consumable ⊑ ... ⊑ BFO:material entity
#   IOF-aligned         DomainClass ⊑ BFO_0000144 ⊑ BFO:process  (carve-out, no cco: intermediate)
#   BFO-only-aligned    DomainClass ⊑ BFO:material entity  (mid-levels bypassed)
#   BFO-only-aligned    DomainClass ⊑ BFO:process  (no carve-out needed)
#   unaligned           DomainClass with no upper-level ancestor
#   IOF-aligned         DomainClass ⊑ iof:PlannedProcess ⊑ BFO:process
#   BFO-only-aligned    B0 contamination: DomainClass ⊑ BFO:material entity
#   IOF-aligned         B1 contamination: DomainClass ⊑ iof:PlannedProcess
#   CCO-aligned         B1 contamination: DomainClass ⊑ cco:Agent ⊑ BFO:material entity
#
# The CCO-before-BFO_0000144 scenario is critical: CCO's Event Ontology
# curates BFO_0000144 and has 12 direct subclasses (cco: namespace).
# A domain class under one of those cco: subclasses is correctly caught
# by priority 1 (CCO-aligned), never reaching the BFO_0000144 carve-out.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
